RHODE ISLAND AMENDATORY ENDORSEMENT
IT IS AGREED THAT this policy is hereby amended to the extent necessary to eliminate any inconsistencies between it and the following provisions: .
Cancellation and Nonrenewal.
1. This policy may be cancelled by the named insured by surrendering this policy to us or any of . our authorized representatives or by mailing to us written notice stating when the cancellation will be effective.
2. This policy may be cancelled by us by giving, mailing or delivering to the named insured and the Agent of Record, if any, at the mailing address shown on the policy, written notice stating the effective date of the cancellation. The specific reason or reasons for the cancellation will be stated only when the named insured requests such a statement in writing, and agrees , in writing, to hold us harmless from liability for any cancellation notice including the stated reasons for cancellation, or for any statement made in connection with an attempt to discover or verify the existence of conditions which would be a reason for cancellation.
3. During the first sixty (60) days of coverage, and if this is not a renewal policy, we may cancel by giving, mailing or delivering to the named insured and the Agent of Record, if any, written notice at least thirty (30) days before or ten (10) days before in the case of nonpayment of premium, of the date of cancellation.
4. After this policy has been in force for sixty (60) days or more, we may cancel this policy prior to the expiration of the policy term only for one of the following specified reasons:
a) Nonpayment of premium ;
b) Discovery of fraud or material misrepresentation made by or with the knowledge of the named insured in obtaining the policy, continuing the policy, or in presenting a claim under the policy;
c) Activities or omissions on the part of the named insured which increase any hazard insured against, including a failure to comply with loss control recommendations;
d) Change in the risk which increases the risk of loss after insurance coverage has been issued or renewed, including but not limited to an increase in exposure due to regulation, legislation, or court decision;
e) Loss or decrease in our reinsurance covering all or part of the risk or exposure covered by this policy;
f) A determination by the Rhode Island Insurance Commissioner that the continuation of the policy would jeopardize our solvency or would place us in violation of the insurance laws of Rhode Island;
