TENNESSEE AMENDATORY ENDORSEMENT
IT IS AGREED that this policy is hereby amended to the extent necessary to eliminate any inconsistencies between it and the following provisions:
Cancellation and Nonrenewal.
1. The first named insured shown in the Declarations may cancel this policy by mailing or delivering to us, or any of our authorized agents, this policy or written notice stating when thereafter the cancellation will be effective.
2. During the first sixty (60) days of coverage and if this is not a renewal policy, we may cancel this policy by mailing to the named insured at the address shown in the policy Declarations, written notice of cancellation at least ten (10) days before the effective date of cancellation.
3. We may cancel this policy if the named insured fails to pay the premium, or any installment on the premium, when due by mailing to the named insured written notice at least ten (10) days before the effective date of cancellation.
4. After this policy has been in force for sixty (60) days or more, or if this is a renewal, other than for non- payment of premium as set out in section 3, we may cancel this policy prior to the expiration of the policy term only for one or more of the following specified reasons: . .
(a) The policy was obtained through a fraud or a material misrepresentation by you in pursuing a claim under this policy or by you and your representative in obtaining this policy;
(b) You have submitted a fraudulent claim;
(c) You have violated or breached any of the terms and conditions of the policy;
(d) The risk originally accepted has substantially increased;
(e) Your conviction of a crime having as one of its necessary elements an act increasing any hazard insured against;
(f) The determination by the Tennessee Director of Insurance that the continuation of the policy could place us in violation of the insurance laws of Tennessee or any other state;
(g) Your failure to comply with written loss control recommendations;
(h) Such other reasons that are approved by the Tennessee Commissioner of Insurance.
Written notice of cancellation provided for the above reasons must be mailed to the named insured at the address shown in the policy at least ten (10) days prior to the effective date of cancellation.
